<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Study Notes</title>

    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background: #f3f0ff;
            padding: 20px;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 850px;
            margin: auto;
            background: white;
            padding: 30px;
            border-radius: 15px;
        }

        h1 {
            text-align: center;
        }

        .note {
            background: #faf9ff;
            padding: 20px;
            margin: 15px 0;
            border-radius: 10px;
        }

        code {
            background: #eee;
            padding: 3px 6px;
            border-radius: 4px;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body>

<div class="container">

    <h1>📝 My Study Notes</h1>

    <div class="note">
        <h2>💻 HTML</h2>
        <p>
            HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language.
            It is used to create the structure of webpages.
        </p>

        <p>
            Example:
            <code>&lt;h1&gt;Hello&lt;/h1&gt;</code>
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="note">
        <h2>🎨 CSS</h2>
        <p>
            CSS stands for Cascading Style Sheets.
            It is used to style and design webpages.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="note">
        <h2>💡 Programming</h2>
        <p>
            Programming means giving instructions to a computer
            to perform specific tasks.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="note">
        <h2>🗃️ Database</h2>
        <p>
            A database is used to store and manage organized information.
        </p>
    </div>

</div>

</body>
</html>
